        {
          "id": 1045486929,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "To see if you're watching?  :-)  \n  \nOn first entry into Endpoints, the Name Resolution checkbox is available even if all name resolution (mac, net, transport) are disabled. Click a different tab (IPv4, TCP, ...) and come back to Ethernet. Now the checkbox is disabled for Name resolution.  \n\nOn entry to Conversations table, name resolution is disabled if none available.  \n  \nI'm open to a better solution - I just copied what was working from Conversations to Endpoints.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
